      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When ARCO built New Cuyama in the 1940s, the town became known as the pearl of eastern Santa Barbara County because of booming oil production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
